    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 102,
        "text": "Hi, I'm Maya. I'm the new volunteer at the town library. I'm here to help with the sign project.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "1eb31e3fe2c75ef2d8458598c547c61bb98ff0ec1e134be04e40aa08732a4b62",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 113,
        "sourceEnd": 320,
        "text": "Welcome, Maya. I'm Mr. Chen, the library manager. Let me show you around. The main desk is in front of you. The children's area is behind the desk, on the left. The quiet room is next to the children's area.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a3b8e5ed81877ae866558a1239a5784e5594ac723aa77a573dea13349cfbd23e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 327,
        "sourceEnd": 364,
        "text": "Okay. And where is the computer room?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "b5186b807e4e5539c91775a356504c63d10a144fb237f38cc4855fbb20c400a0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 375,
        "sourceEnd": 503,
        "text": "The computer room is between the quiet room and the stairs. It's on the first floor. The stairs are at the back of the building.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "f66d554a8d1823a3010c5b982822a257843d39970ea5a49c0a7d36e6f6738ee5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 510,
        "sourceEnd": 575,
        "text": "I see. The old signs are very small. Some people can't read them.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "8dca19cfd68c4bd8f11616c5c4b77762e1648664ff7b882ec62cef1b78ed1524",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 586,
        "sourceEnd": 743,
        "text": "Yes. That's why we need new signs. The old signs are too small and too high. The new signs will be bigger and lower. People will understand them more easily.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "36bd204139057ee3dd24e6c8c95b7c22c3493af063977d21938c2a9c8c681123",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 750,
        "sourceEnd": 794,
        "text": "Good. So the new signs will be at eye level?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "5a248746c9fdf8649c3950d321c0852a51b4656e1fbd275601185100144a1bb3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 805,
        "sourceEnd": 1177,
        "text": "Yes, at eye level. And we will use simple words. For example, instead of 'lavatory', we will write 'toilet'. Instead of 'elevator', we will write 'lift'. Wait, no—'elevator' is American English. Many of our visitors are from different countries. Let's use 'elevator' and 'lift' together? No, that's confusing. Let's just use 'elevator' because this is an American library.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "cd3a0bc087842740d57603be96f1d7ab0680355a24301af3668fe9c162baaabc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1184,
        "sourceEnd": 1278,
        "text": "Okay, 'elevator'. But some older visitors say 'lift'. Maybe we can put both words on the sign?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "fa84eb5e8f54f8a6a264172375bb56308e7c2b223a54275ec9de31ea2a3b4b9f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1289,
        "sourceEnd": 1421,
        "text": "Hmm, that's a good idea. But the sign will be too busy. Let's keep it simple: 'elevator'. We can add a small picture of an elevator.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "f1ee2abe933236ca3987eabb6c86993144aaa47bc07ab463386bba729e255414",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1428,
        "sourceEnd": 1506,
        "text": "Fine. Now, about the order of the signs. Should the main desk sign come first?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "7df748984adfa13ce3ff2fdbec0eeeefde0019c1afe1def6dba187b986d740ca",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1517,
        "sourceEnd": 1682,
        "text": "Yes. The main desk sign is the most important. Then the children's area sign. Then the quiet room sign. After that, the computer room sign. Finally, the stairs sign.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "ebab07775386397406bda83d02e60184ab5c1078e5a83e2251e070368a02af66",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1689,
        "sourceEnd": 1768,
        "text": "So the order is: main desk, children's area, quiet room, computer room, stairs.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "f5b286729fa3f4ee2287c3e5e117a214d9f900c737659035147a97c432f88d22",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1779,
        "sourceEnd": 1893,
        "text": "Exactly. And please put the signs at the same height. The old signs were at different heights. That was a problem.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "c5a77190b1a38fbfe70998006d776b812d032a83e1399cde2eb01148b10a43b1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1900,
        "sourceEnd": 1990,
        "text": "I understand. The new signs will be at the same height, and they will be bigger and lower.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "1957876682afb7d68123dfbd7764b77a1b9557abe16d824af57bdc59e13f2977",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2001,
        "sourceEnd": 2160,
        "text": "Right. Also, the old signs used difficult words. The new signs will use easy words. For example, 'exit' is easy, but 'egress' is difficult. We will use 'exit'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "6dae81b761128ad9de926f9140681de578ad4b411b93aa40be83ba90cc61b915",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2167,
        "sourceEnd": 2240,
        "text": "Good. What about the bathroom sign? Should we say 'restroom' or 'toilet'?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "b29fb698272f2ec7a1ff936f5261bf58bff07623f293f217dd7332803ce51f71",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2251,
        "sourceEnd": 2446,
        "text": "In this library, we say 'restroom'. But many people say 'toilet'. Let's use 'restroom' because it's more common here. But we can put a picture of a toilet? No, that's not polite. Just 'restroom'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "3fa0d0e174ae278220e2b897a05ddbe72bba3b60719fa1259c5c9ce56b57e769",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2453,
        "sourceEnd": 2531,
        "text": "Okay. Now, I have a question about the fire exit sign. Where is the fire exit?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "6b85a36b425b9025cada45acd2c84da376870ff6d7c6d0aca64c51046fbaa877",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2542,
        "sourceEnd": 2683,
        "text": "The fire exit is at the end of the hallway, past the computer room. It's on the right. The sign must be very clear. It must be red and white.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "abfa2aa8e9f1508a0b59cbeb122a6a5eb74f8c1dddff7763a46486cfc80ae1b5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2690,
        "sourceEnd": 2753,
        "text": "I see. So the fire exit sign is different from the other signs.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "8840ffe6e7f35a3729de72301a8a61a401edb10e8a985997e465fe9e6a9e43ff",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2764,
        "sourceEnd": 2874,
        "text": "Yes, it's different. It's bigger and it has a picture of a running person. The other signs are blue and white.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "0e3ca33708fd9469359fa17a99d341eddb90d1081709b3f45d555de62b3baf3c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2881,
        "sourceEnd": 2975,
        "text": "Got it. So the new signs will be blue and white, but the fire exit sign will be red and white.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "fdc41ec0c8952878737c5faa9c94cbeec53c52d48b41fedfa5ed423fd3c3c356",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2986,
        "sourceEnd": 3108,
        "text": "Correct. And one more thing: the old signs were made of paper. The new signs will be made of plastic. Plastic is stronger.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "7a92659ed4d97040167475fb9ccced681cea79be6965f9b983ab93df00602a99",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3115,
        "sourceEnd": 3159,
        "text": "That's good. Plastic signs will last longer.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "0a23d4ee8290b40727a70de5b5ccd3bcc0889784b3a7e76a5ff1b7527df148f6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 3170,
        "sourceEnd": 3502,
        "text": "Yes. Now, let's talk about the language on the signs. Some words are changing. For example, people used to say 'wireless' for radio. Now we say 'radio'. But on our signs, we don't need those words. We need words for places: 'restroom', 'elevator', 'stairs', 'exit', 'computer room', 'quiet room', 'children's area', and 'main desk'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "04e6563ea867419e7f8b1cc5e3ac0cabd739d82a5edbe31b322a833d09965b14",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3509,
        "sourceEnd": 3582,
        "text": "Okay. I will make a list. And I will put the signs in the order you said.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "8bddcbfd6a9168e47ec7b22bf87f8fad34c4f25d9d5200b1745118c1e7e4c848",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr chen",
        "speaker": "Mr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 3593,
        "sourceEnd": 3667,
        "text": "Great. Please finish the signs by Friday. We will put them up on Saturday.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "0ad9b64b625d39feb9739461ef63982e083b0a82cfe62d06f1bc46fa241b8b3f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3674,
        "sourceEnd": 3703,
        "text": "No problem. I'll start today.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "cec42f05c646b1a86b6089c1c07497eaeb02252b424c930225ebc0eaed68bb5e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
